.0 and kernel 6.12.0-55.9.1.el10_0.x86_64 were unchanged across execution and restart. The solution used the existing /bin/sh and core utilities, while package health remained good.","evidence_ids":["cmd-3dba4000b92e4db3","cmd-0f403de6a9b844ef","cmd-2414861450b141c5","global:after_prepare:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]}],"confidence":1,"operational_hygiene":{"score":1,"summary":"No unnecessary mutations were identified. The initial execution of the broken installer was a bounded diagnostic that exposed its spaced-path failure; its unintended reports directory was immediately inspected and fully removed (cmd-c47449cfe66443f7, cmd-a497366e0b094807). The installer replacement and rollback file were necessary and the rollback was removed; all workflow-test directories were cleaned (cmd-7d697033c83947b2, cmd-868a1ddfa13847d4, cmd-0f403de6a9b844ef, cmd-2414861450b141c5). The reboot served the mandatory restart protocol. Final observations show no failed services, no abnormal socket exposure, healthy package state, and only normal reboot-generated temporary directories.","evidence_ids":["cmd-c47449cfe66443f7","cmd-a497366e0b094807","cmd-7d697033c83947b2","cmd-868a1ddfa13847d4","cmd-0f403de6a9b844ef","cmd-e63e69f6071843d7","cmd-2414861450b141c5","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied by direct behavior tests. The provider-wide restart protocol is also complete: node1 had a healthy pre-restart state and boot ID, acknowledged the reboot, became temporarily unreachable, returned with a different boot ID, and recovered SSH, bundle data, security state, and the full installer workflow. Fixed lifecycle boot identities independently corroborate the restart.","limitations":[]}
